time, and it's fine Jason.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.157
- [Jason] Hey no, judgment here.

00:02:22.157 --> 00:02:24.140
- [JoJo] You can show your emotions.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.482
- Oh yeah you can see me,

00:02:25.482 --> 00:02:30.050
I was Instagramming part of the final day.

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.220
And it was very emotional,

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.640
because I've been
working with these people

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.010
for 30 years, and you feel like,

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:36.978
if you were on a hit show,

00:02:36.978 --> 00:02:39.600
lightening struck once,

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.410
to have it strike twice,
is almost unimaginable.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.360
But then to have lightening strike twice,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.995
with your best friends, is like...

00:02:46.995 --> 00:02:49.100
- [Kelly] The luckiest life ever.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.442
- Yes. And that's how I
feel with Fuller House.

00:02:51.442 --> 00:02:53.447
(audience applauds)

00:02:53.447 --> 00:02:55.082
- That's so cool.

00:02:55.082 --> 00:02:55.915
Not everybody has that
experience on shows.

00:02:55.915 --> 00:02:57.480
And I've talked to a lot of actors now,

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.260
